# TEST IMAGE ONLY -- bring the out-of-band management port up at boot.
#
# The management NIC is deliberately kept out of the dataplane: the suites open
# by running "delete interfaces dataplane", which would otherwise take the
# management path down with them. dataplane.conf excludes ens30 and ens31 for
# that reason.
#
# Being outside the dataplane also puts it outside the DANOS CLI, which models
# dataplane, loopback, bridge, bonding and tunnel interfaces and nothing else.
# There is no "set interfaces ens31" to write, so this cannot be part of a
# configuration the CLI owns and has to be here instead.
#
# It used to be done at prep time, with "sudo dhclient ens31" over the console.
# That stopped working when the image went back to booting into the CLI
# sandbox, where sudo, ip and dhclient are all out of reach -- and it was the
# wrong place regardless: a real deployment brings its management port up on
# its own, before anyone logs in, not as a step in a test script.
#
# allow-hotplug rather than auto, and both slots listed, so one image serves a
# one-NIC and a two-NIC management setup: a slot that is not present simply
# never fires, where "auto" on a missing interface fails networking.service.

allow-hotplug ens30
iface ens30 inet dhcp

allow-hotplug ens31
iface ens31 inet dhcp
